---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { repoBlob } from "../../lib/links.mjs";
---

<DocsLayout title="Skills — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1>Skills</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Agent-loaded procedures ship with the distro: <code>AGENTS.md</code> is a
      short role bootstrap every session loads, <code>COORDINATOR.md</code> is
      the coordinator core init names, and each action's detail stays in the
      bundled skills, loaded only for that action.
    </p>
    <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule)">
      <div class="kv lg" style="grid-template-columns:160px 1fr">
        <div class="k">/sum-dispatch</div>
        <div class="v">
          Send one approved request to a worker. Creates the task brief,
          prepares a separate Herdr worktree, launches the selected worker,
          submits its brief, and returns control to you.
        </div>
        <div class="k">/sum-work</div>
        <div class="v">
          Do that task in its own Herdr worktree. A worker is explicitly given
          its own role; it does not become another coordinator.
        </div>
        <div class="k">/sum-deliver</div>
        <div class="v">
          Run the project's checks and prepare the PR. Verification and PR
          delivery through the nine gates.
        </div>
        <div class="k">/sum-status</div>
        <div class="v">
          Reconcile saved tasks and pending returns. Finds workers that stopped
          without a report.
        </div>
        <div class="k">/sum-develop</div>
        <div class="v">
          Change sum from a development checkout that cannot claim the
          coordinator.
        </div>
        <div class="k">/sum-factory</div>
        <div class="v">
          Start or run a factory from a markdown settings file. Software and
          copy differ only in that file.
        </div>
        <div class="k" style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">
          /sum-update
        </div>
        <div class="v" style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">
          Update or roll back the installation, then refresh running sessions.
          Atomic updates with rolling session refresh and code-only rollback.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Factory lane</h2>
      <p>
        A factory lane (<code>sumctl factory</code> plus the factory procedures
        in sum-dispatch and the worker procedure) can run sequential ready
        issues on an enrolled project without a sum daemon: tick is a one-shot
        helper, dispatch stays with the coordinator, and merge happens only at
        high confidence on authorized repositories.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Third-party skills</h2>
      <div class="codeblock">
        <div>./bin/sumctl skills install ...</div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Delegates explicit skill and agent selections to the pinned Vercel
        Skills CLI in project copy mode. Skills reach agents as explicit file
        references (path, size, hash) to read when needed, not as an assumed
        skill standard. See <a href={repoBlob("docs/sum-skills.md")}
          >docs/sum-skills.md ↗</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Verification authoring skills</h2>
      <p>
        <code>.agents/skills/create-verification</code> inspects a repository,
        scaffolds its contract, verify task, seed feature maps, and vendored
        skills without inventing commands, then proves them once; <code
          >.agents/skills/maintain-verification</code
        > audits stale tasks, paths, links, and coverage claims. Both work in
        any clone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
